   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I am plotting a <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">ggplot2</code> graph that has an uneven number of facets. My plot currently looks something like this:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">library(ggplot2)\r\n\r\ndf &lt;- data.frame(group=c(1,1,2,2,3),\r\n                 name=c(&#39;a&#39;,&#39;b&#39;,&#39;c&#39;,&#39;d&#39;,&#39;e&#39;),\r\n                 x=c(1,2,3,4,5),\r\n                 y=c(2,3,4,5,6))\r\nggplot(df, aes(x,y)) + geom_point() + facet_wrap(~ name, ncol=3)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Note that the default positioning for the facets is:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">a b c\r\nd e\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">However, I would like to have a finer control on the positioning of the facets. Specifically, I would like to “center” the bottom two facets in order to distribute the void space more evenly on the sides of the plot.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">In other words, the ideal placement for me would look like:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">a b c\r\n d e\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Is this something that can be achieved with <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">ggplot2</code>? How? Many thanks in advance.</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj5JIGFtIHBsb3R0aW5nIGEgYGdncGxvdDJgIGdyYXBoIHRoYXQgaGFzIGFuIHVuZXZlbiBu\r\ndW1iZXIgb2YgZmFjZXRzLiBNeSBwbG90IGN1cnJlbnRseSBsb29rcyBzb21ldGhpbmcgbGlrZSB0\r\naGlzOjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+YGBgPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5saWJyYXJ5KGdncGxv\r\ndDIpPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5kZiAmbHQ7LSBkYXRhLmZyYW1lKGdyb3VwPWMo\r\nMSwxLDIsMiwzKSw8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsg\r\nJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7bmFtZT1jKCdhJywnYicsJ2MnLCdkJywnZScpLDwv\r\nZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7\r\nICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDt4PWMoMSwyLDMsNCw1KSw8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5i\r\nc3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7eT1jKDIsMyw0LDUs\r\nNikpPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5nZ3Bsb3QoZGYsIGFlcyh4LHkpKSArIGdlb21fcG9pbnQoKSArIGZhY2V0\r\nX3dyYXAofiBuYW1lLCBuY29sPTM