     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, August 20, 2020 at 1:24:04 PM UTC-3 Ben Bolker wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div>\r\n    <p>   I very much doubt it: I would check out the cowplot and\r\n      patchwork packages.  In principle you can use these tools to do\r\n      things like delete redundant axes, align plots, and place them how\r\n      you want, but I expect it will be a nuisance.<br>\r\n    </p></div><div>\r\n    <div>On 8/20/20 12:15 PM, &#39;Thiago V. dos\r\n      Santos&#39; via ggplot2 wrote:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    </div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      \r\n      <div>\r\n        <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I am plotting a <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">ggplot2</code>\r\n          graph that has an uneven number of facets. My plot currently\r\n          looks something like this:</p>\r\n        <pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">library(ggplot2)\r\n\r\ndf &lt;- data.frame(group=c(1,1,2,2,3),\r\n                 name=c(&#39;a&#39;,&#39;b&#39;,&#39;c&#39;,&#39;d&#39;,&#39;e&#39;),\r\n                 x=c(1,2,3,4,5),\r\n                 y=c(2,3,4,5,6))\r\nggplot(df, aes(x,y)) + geom_point() + facet_wrap(~ name, ncol=3)\r\n</code></pre>\r\n        <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Note that the\r\n          default positioning for the facets is:</p>\r\n        <pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">a b c\r\nd e\r\n</code></pre>\r\n        <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">However, I would\r\n          like to have a finer control on the positioning of the facets.\r\n          Specifically, I would like to “center” the bottom two facets\r\n          in order to distribute the void space more evenly on the sides\r\n          of the plot.</p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">In other words, the\r\n          ideal placement for me would look like:</p>\r\n        <pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline;white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">a b c\r\n d e\r\n</code></pre>\r\n        <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Is this something\r\n          that can be achieved with <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">ggplot2</code>?\r\n          How? Many thanks in advance.</p>\r\n        <div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj5JIGFtIHBsb3R0aW5nIGEgYGdncGxvdDJgIGdyYXBoIHRoYXQgaGFzIGFuIHVuZXZlbiBudW1iZXIgb2YgZmFjZXRzLiBNeSBwbG90IGN1cnJlbnRseSBsb29rcyBzb21ldGhpbmcgbGlrZSB0\r\naGlzOjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+YGBgPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5saWJyYXJ5KGdncGxv\r\ndDIpPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5kZiAmbHQ7LSBkYXRhLmZyYW1lKGdyb3VwPWMo\r\nMSwxLDIsMiwzKSw8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsg\r\nJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7bmFtZT1jKCdhJywnYicsJ2MnLCdkJywnZScpLDwv\r\nZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7\r\nICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDt4PWMoMSwyLDMsNCw1KSw8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5i\r\nc3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7eT1jKDIsMyw0LDUs\r\nNikpPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5nZ3Bsb3QoZGYsIGFlcyh4LHkpKSArIGdlb21fcG9pbnQoKSArIGZhY2V0\r\nX3dyYXAofiBuYW1lLCBuY29sPTMpJm5ic3A7PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5gYGA8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48\r\nL2Rpdj48ZGl2Pk5vdGUgdGhhdCB0aGUgZGVmYXVsdCBwb3NpdGlvbmluZyBmb3IgdGhlIGZhY2V0\r\ncyBpczo8YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5gYGA8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PmEgYiBjPC9k\r\naXY+PGRpdj5kIGU8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PmBgYDwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+SG93ZXZl\r\nciwgSSB3b3VsZCBsaWtlIHRvIGhhdmUgYSBmaW5lciBjb250cm9sIG9uIHRoZSBwb3NpdGlvbmlu\r\nZyBvZiB0aGUgZmFjZXRzLiBTcGVjaWZpY2FsbHksIEkgd291bGQgbGlrZSB0byAiY2VudGVyIiB0\r\naGUgYm90dG9tIHR3byBmYWNldHMgaW4gb3JkZXIgdG8gZGlzdHJpYnV0ZSB0aGUgdm9pZCBzcGFj\r\nZSBtb3JlIGV2ZW5seSBvbiB0aGUgc2lkZXMgb2YgdGhlIHBsb3QuPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9k\r\naXY+PGRpdj5JbiBvdGhlciB3b3JkcywgdGhlIGlkZWFsIHBsYWNlbWVudCBmb3IgbWUgd291bGQg\r\nbG9vayBsaWtlOjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+YGBgPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5hIGIgYzwv\r\nZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7ZCBlPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5gYGA8L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2\r\nPklzIHRoaXMgc29tZXRoaW5nIHRoYXQgY2FuIGJlIGFjaGlldmVkIHdpdGggYGdncGxvdDJgPyBI\r\n          b3c/IE1hbnkgdGhhbmtzIGluIGFkdmFuY2UuPC9kaXY+\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;